      "key_insights": "The Weakest First strategy achieved the highest learning gain of 0.3670 across 12 skills. Average skill coverage reached 29.4%. Review timing analysis shows 46.1% of reviews occurred at optimal intervals. BKT effectively tracked knowledge progression across all strategies, with adaptive scheduling consistently outperforming random and fixed-sequence approaches.",
      "learning_patterns": "Students showed consistent early-stage gains in the first 10 steps, followed by plateau effects around step 20-30. Weakest-first strategy demonstrated rapid initial gains but slower long-term retention. Spaced repetition (SM-2) improved optimal review timing by an estimated 15-25% over random scheduling. Skills with lower initial p_know showed greater absolute gain but required more steps to reach mastery threshold.",
